    <innerclass refid="classapi_1_1v2_1_1Doc" prot="public">api::v2::Doc</innerclass>
    <innernamespace refid="namespaceapi">api</innernamespace>
    <innernamespace refid="namespaceapi_1_1v2">api::v2</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Serves the Swagger UI page that documents the API. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This file defines the Doc controller with a single endpoint. That endpoint returns an HTML page containing the Swagger UI, an interactive documentation viewer for the REST API. The HTML is embedded into the program at build time from docs/api.html, so the running server does not need to read any file from disk. The handler simply builds a 200 HTML response and hands it to the callback; there is no per-request state or authentication.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: This is the human-facing documentation endpoint of the API. Developers and testers open it in a browser to see every available route, its parameters and its response format. Drogon calls it at the /api/v2/doc URL; it uses no database and no controllers. Because it goes through the INSECURE chain it is rate-limited and timed but needs no token, so anyone can read the public docs.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Swagger / OpenAPI: a standard way to describe REST APIs (<ulink url="https://swagger.io/">https://swagger.io/</ulink>).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>HTTP GET and status 200: <ulink url="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Methods">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Methods</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>CORS: <ulink url="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/CORS">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/CORS</ulink></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
